00:14:52.640 --> 00:14:55.760
And we get all cold, shivery,

261
00:14:55.760 --> 00:14:58.720
and everything just starts feeling droopy.

262
00:14:58.730 --> 00:15:00.890
Hey, hey. Hey, easy.

263
00:15:00.890 --> 00:15:02.690
Why are you crying?

264
00:15:03.100 --> 00:15:06.240
It's just like really the opposite of what we're going for here.

265
00:15:06.690 --> 00:15:08.190
Crying helps me slow down,

266
00:15:08.190 --> 00:15:11.030
and obsess over the weight of life's problems.

267
00:15:12.320 --> 00:15:14.740
You know what? Let's, think about something else.

268
00:15:14.740 --> 00:15:18.790
How about we read some mind manuals, huh? Sounds fun.

269
00:15:18.790 --> 00:15:20.330
I've read most of them.

270
00:15:20.330 --> 00:15:22.120
Well, have you read this one? This seems interesting.

271
00:15:22.120 --> 00:15:25.290
"Long term memory retrieval, volume 47"?

272
00:15:25.290 --> 00:15:27.670
- No.  - A real page-turner!

273
00:15:27.670 --> 00:15:31.550
"Long term memory data selection via channel subgrouping"?

274
00:15:31.550 --> 00:15:34.260
See? Fun already! You lucky dog.

275
00:15:34.260 --> 00:15:36.000
You're reading these cool things.

276
00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:37.980
I got to go work. Life is so unfair.

277
00:15:47.110 --> 00:15:48.240
What can we do?

278
00:15:48.240 --> 00:15:50.690
We've only got capital to last a month, maybe two.

279
00:15:50.690 --> 00:15:52.430
If we can't find investors by then,

280
00:15:52.440 --> 00:15:54.360
we're going to have to lay people off.

281
00:15:54.360 --> 00:15:57.700
Mom! Dad! Come kiss me good night!

282
00:15:57.700 --> 00:15:59.080
- I know. I know.  - Be right there!

283
00:15:59.080 --> 00:16:01.380
We've got to land this, okay?

284
00:16:03.370 --> 00:16:05.750
Did you hear dad? He sounded really upset.

285
00:16:08.840 --> 00:16:11.010
What was that? Was it a bear? It's a bear!

286
00:16:11.010 --> 00:16:12.550
There are no bears in San Francisco.

287
00:16:12.550 --> 00:16:14.760
I saw a really hairy guy. He looked like a bear.

288
00:16:14.760 --> 00:16:17.140
I'm so jumpy. My nerves are shot.

289
00:16:17.420 --> 00:16:18.920
I don't want to hear about your nerves.

290
00:16:18.920 --> 00:16:19.820
I'll tell you what it is.

291
00:16:19.820 --> 00:16:21.660
This move has been a bust.

292
00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:23.070
That's what I've been telling you guys!

293
00:16:23.070 --> 00:16:25.580
There are at least 37 things for Riley to be scared of right now.

294
00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:27.310
The smell alone is enough to make her gag.

295
00:16:27.310 --> 00:16:29.260
I can't believe mom and dad moved us here!

296
00:16:29.260 --> 00:16:31.710
Look, I get it. You guys have concerns.

297
00:16:31.710 --> 00:16:33.170
But we've been through worse!

298
00:16:33.170 --> 00:16:34.570
Tell you what, let's make a list

299
00:16:34.570 --> 00:16:36.920
of all the things Riley should be happy about.

300
00:16:36.920 --> 00:16:39.720
Fine. Let's see, this house stinks, our room stinks.

301
00:16:39.720 --> 00:16:41.890
- Pizza is weird here.  - Our friends are back home.

302
00:16:41.890 --> 00:16:43.600
And all of our stuff is in the missing van!

303
00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:45.430
Come on. It could be worse.

304
00:16:45.430 --> 00:16:46.140
Yeah, Joy.

305
00:16:46.140 --> 00:16:49.060
We could be lying on the dirty floor. In a bag.

306
00:16:49.060 --> 00:16:51.020
Okay, I admit it, we had a rough start.

307
00:16:51.020 --> 00:16:52.460
But think of all the good things that...

308
00:16:52.460 --> 00:16:53.180
No, Joy.

309
00:16:53.180 --> 00:16:56.280
There's absolutely no reason for Riley to be happy right now.

310
00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:57.570
Let us handle this.

311
00:16:57.570 --> 00:17:00.070
I say we skip school tomorrow and lock ourselves in the bedroom.

312
00:17:00.070 --> 00:17:01.910
We have no clean clothes. I mean, no one should see us.

313
00:17:01.910 --> 00:17:03.700
Yeah, we could cry until we can't breathe.

314
00:17:03.700 --> 00:17:06.360
We should lock the door and scream that curse word we know.

315
00:17:06.360 --> 00:17:08.250
- It's a good one!  - Now hold on!

316
00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:11.290
Look, we all have our off days. You know...

317
00:17:11.290 --> 00:17:12.420
Hi, honey.

318
00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:15.350
The mom bad news train is pulling in.

319
00:17:16.590 --> 00:17:18.590
Still no moving Van.

320
00:17:18.590 --> 00:17:20.450
Now they're saying it won't be here till Tuesday,

321
00:17:20.450 --> 00:17:21.310
can you believe it?

322
00:17:22.260 --> 00:17:23.390
Where's dad?

323
00:17:23.390 --> 00:17:26.600
On the phone. This new venture is keeping him pretty busy.

324
00:17:26.600 --> 00:17:28.140
I rest my case!

325
00:17:28.140 --> 00:17:30.060
Your dad's a little stressed,

326
00:17:30.060 --> 00:17:32.160
you know, about getting his new company up and running.

327
00:17:32.160 --> 00:17:34.570
Now for a few well-placed withering scowls.

328
00:17:36.060 --> 00:17:38.690
I guess all I really want to say is,

329
00:17:38.810 --> 00:17:40.030
thank you.

330
00:17:40.030 --> 00:17:44.490
You know, through all this confusion you've stayed...

331
00:17:44.490 --> 00:17:46.330
Well, you've stayed our happy girl.

332
00:17:47.410 --> 00:17:49.210
Your dad's under a lot of pressure,

333
00:17:49.620 --> 00:17:52.170
but if you and I can keep smiling,

334
00:17:52.170 --> 00:17:53.910
it would be a big help.

335
00:17:53.910 --> 00:17:56.470
We can do that for him. Right?

336
00:18:01.970 --> 00:18:03.310
Yeah, sure.

337
00:18:03.800 --> 00:18:05.550
What did we do to deserve you?

338
00:18:09.560 --> 00:18:11.360
- Sweet dreams.  - Good night.

339
00:18:12.940 --> 00:18:15.150
Well, you can't argue with mom. Happy it is.

340
00:18:15.150 --> 00:18:16.400
Team Happy! Sounds great!

341
00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:17.580
Totally behind you, Joy.

342
00:18:19.070 --> 00:18:20.900
Looks like we're going into rem.

343
00:18:20.900 --> 00:18:21.870
I got dream duty,

344
00:18:21.870 --> 00:18:23.860
so I'll take care of sending these to Long Term.

345
00:18:23.860 --> 00:18:25.650
Great day today, guys!

346
00:18:25.650 --> 00:18:28.120
Sleep well, Team Happy!

347
00:18:29.160 --> 00:18:31.550
All right, what's on tonight, Dream Production?

348
00:18:37.500 --> 00:18:39.250
Well, this is it. The new place.

349
00:18:42.510 --> 00:18:44.850
Come live with me, Riley.

350
00:18:45.550 --> 00:18:47.640
Somebody order a broccoli pizza?

351
00:18:47.640 --> 00:18:49.270
-Eat me!  -I'm organic!

352
00:18:51.010 --> 00:18:54.140
No! Who is in charge of programing down there?

353
00:18:54.220 --> 00:18:56.190
I know I'm not supposed to do this, but...

354
00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:03.500
We are not going to end the day like this.

355
00:19:47.360 --> 00:19:48.860
don't you worry.

356
00:19:48.860 --> 00:19:52.910
I'm gonna make sure that tomorrow is another great day.

357
00:19:52.910 --> 00:19:54.830
I promise.

358
00:20:07.470 --> 00:20:08.930
Hello! Did I wake you?

359
00:20:08.930 --> 00:20:10.050
Do you have to play that?

360
00:20:10.050 --> 00:20:11.350
Well, I have to practice.

361
00:20:11.350 --> 00:20:14.030
And I don't think of it as playing so much as hugging.

362
00:20:15.730 --> 00:20:17.730
First day of school! Very, very exciting.

363
00:20:17.730 --> 00:20:20.100
I was up late last night figuring out a new plan.

364
00:20:20.100 --> 00:20:21.230
Here it is! Fear.

365
00:20:21.230 --> 00:20:23.820
I need a list of all the possible negative outcomes

366
00:20:23.820 --> 00:20:25.110
on the first day at a new school.

367
00:20:25.110 --> 00:20:25.980
Way ahead of you there.

368
00:20:25.980 --> 00:20:27.450
Does anyone know how to spell "Meteor"?

369
00:20:27.450 --> 00:20:29.610
Disgust. Make sure Riley stands out today.

370
00:20:29.610 --> 00:20:30.910
But also blends in.

371
00:20:30.910 --> 00:20:32.780
When I'm through, Riley will look so good,

372
00:20:32.780 --> 00:20:34.950
the other kids will look at their own outfits and barf.

373
00:20:34.950 --> 00:20:36.120
"Joy." "Yes, Joy?"

374
00:20:36.120 --> 00:20:37.620
"You'll be in charge of the console,

375
00:20:37.620 --> 00:20:39.080
keeping Riley happy all day long.

376
00:20:39.080 --> 00:20:40.790
"And may I add I love your dress? It's adorable."

377
00:20:40.790 --> 00:20:42.250
"This old thing? Thank you so much.

378
00:20:42.260 --> 00:20:43.890
I love the way it twirls."

379
00:20:44.420 --> 00:20:46.600
Train of Thought! Right on schedule.

380
00:20:48.470 --> 00:20:50.550
Anger. Unload the daydreams.

381
00:20:50.550 --> 00:20:52.760
I ordered extra in case things get slow in class.

382
00:20:52.760 --> 00:20:53.800
It might come in handy.

383
00:20:53.800 --> 00:20:56.140
If this new school is full of boring, useless classes.

384
00:20:56.140 --> 00:20:57.810
Which it probably will be.

385
00:20:57.810 --> 00:21:01.520
Sadness. I have a super important job just for you.

386
00:21:01.520 --> 00:21:03.730
- Really?  - Follow me.

387
00:21:05.820 --> 00:21:08.280
- What are you doing?  - And there. Perfect!

388
00:21:08.280 --> 00:21:10.400
This is the circle of sadness.

389
00:21:10.400 --> 00:21:12.110
Your job is to make sure

390
00:21:12.110 --> 00:21:14.950
that all the sadness stays inside of it.

391
00:21:14.950 --> 00:21:17.790
So you want me to just stand here?

392
00:21:17.790 --> 00:21:21.080
Hey, it's not my place to tell you how to do your job.

393
00:21:21.080 --> 00:21:25.630
Just make sure that all the sadness stays in the circle!

394
00:21:25.630 --> 00:21:28.960
See? You're a pro at this! Isn't this fun?

395
00:21:28.960 --> 00:21:30.170
- No.  - Atta girl.

396
00:21:30.170 --> 00:21:31.470
All right, everyone, fresh start.

397
00:21:31.470 --> 00:21:32.500
We are gonna have a good day,

398
00:21:32.500 --> 00:21:33.590
which will turn into a good week,

399
00:21:33.590 --> 00:21:34.550
which will turn into a good year,

400
00:21:34.550 --> 00:21:36.010
which turns into a good life!

401
00:21:36.220 --> 00:21:37.510
So, the big day!

402
00:21:37.510 --> 00:21:39.270
New school, new friends, huh?

403
00:21:39.270 --> 00:21:41.850
I know! I'm kind of nervous, but I'm mostly excited.

404
00:21:41.850 --> 00:21:43.270
How do I look? Do you like my shirt?

405
00:21:43.270 --> 00:21:44.980
Very cute!

406
00:21:44.980 --> 00:21:46.650
Are you gonna be okay? You want us to walk with you?

407
00:21:46.650 --> 00:21:48.570
Mom and dad? With us in public?

408
00:21:48.570 --> 00:21:50.030
- No thank you.  - I'm on it!

409
00:21:50.030 --> 00:21:52.620
Nope! I'm fine. Bye, mom. Bye, dad.

410
00:21:52.820 --> 00:21:54.450
Have a good day at school, Monkey.

411
00:21:59.750 --> 00:22:01.460
Have a great day, sweetheart!

412
00:22:01.540 --> 00:22:04.300
-That's crazy. It really is.  -That was so funny.

413
00:22:05.670 --> 00:22:07.600
Do you know what basketball game is coming up?

414
00:22:08.050 --> 00:22:09.210
Are you sure we want to do this?

415
00:22:09.210 --> 00:22:12.050
- In we go!  - Okay! Going in! Yes!

416
00:22:16.010 --> 00:22:17.510
Did you see her? Hello?

417
00:22:17.510 --> 00:22:19.970
Okay, we've got a group of cool girls at two o'clock.

418
00:22:19.970 --> 00:22:20.540
How do you know?

419
00:22:20.540 --> 00:22:22.390
Double ears pierced, infinity scarf.

420
00:22:22.390 --> 00:22:23.790
Is she wearing eye shadow?

421
00:22:23.790 --> 00:22:25.270
Yeah, we want to be friends with them.

422
00:22:25.270 --> 00:22:26.110
Let's go talk to them!

423
00:22:26.110 --> 00:22:27.730
Are you kidding? We're not talking to them.

424
00:22:27.730 --> 00:22:29.150
We want them to like us.

425
00:22:29.150 --> 00:22:30.570
Yeah. Wait, what?

426
00:22:30.570 --> 00:22:32.570
Almost finished with the potential disasters.

427
00:22:32.570 --> 00:22:36.070
Worst scenario is either quicksand, spontaneous combustion,

428
00:22:36.070 --> 00:22:37.740
or getting called on by the teacher.

429
00:22:37.740 --> 00:22:39.540
So as long as none of those happen...

430
00:22:39.540 --> 00:22:42.000
Okay, everybody. We have a new student in class today.

431
00:22:42.000 --> 00:22:44.290
Are you kidding me? Out of the gate?

432
00:22:44.290 --> 00:22:45.540
This is not happening!

433
00:22:45.540 --> 00:22:48.250
Riley, would you like to tell us something about yourself?

434
00:22:48.250 --> 00:22:49.290
No!

435
00:22:49.290 --> 00:22:50.590
Pretend we can't speak English.

436
00:22:50.590 --> 00:22:51.810
don't worry. I got this.

437
00:22:53.760 --> 00:22:54.930
Okay.

438
00:22:54.930 --> 00:22:56.550
My name is Riley Andersen.

439
00:22:56.550 --> 00:22:59.810
I'm from Minnesota and now I live here.

440
00:23:02.220 --> 00:23:04.440
And how about Minnesota?

441
00:23:04.440 --> 00:23:05.900
Can you tell us something about it?

442
00:23:05.900 --> 00:23:08.030
Well, you certainly get a lot more snow than we do.

443
00:23:10.360 --> 00:23:12.160
She's hilarious!

444
00:23:13.280 --> 00:23:15.280
Yeah, it gets pretty cold.

445
00:23:15.280 --> 00:23:17.780
The lake freezes over, and that's when we play hockey.

446
00:23:17.780 --> 00:23:20.120
I'm on a great team. We're called the Prairie Dogs.

447
00:23:20.120 --> 00:23:23.120
My friend Meg plays forward. And my dad's the coach.

448
00:23:23.120 --> 00:23:25.750
Pretty much everyone in my family skates.

449
00:23:25.750 --> 00:23:27.630
It's kind of a family tradition.

450
00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:29.430
We go out on the lake almost every weekend.

451
00:23:32.710 --> 00:23:35.130
Or we did, till I moved away.

452
00:23:35.130 --> 00:23:36.300
- Hey, what gives?  - Wait, what?

453
00:23:37.170 --> 00:23:38.920
Sadness! You touched a memory?

454
00:23:38.920 --> 00:23:40.600
We talked about this.

455
00:23:40.600 --> 00:23:42.310
Yeah, I know. I'm sorry.

456
00:23:42.310 --> 00:23:43.980
Get back in your circle.

457
00:23:43.980 --> 00:23:45.100
What's going on?

458
00:23:45.100 --> 00:23:47.190
- Why won't it eject?  - Get it out of there, Joy.

459
00:23:47.270 --> 00:23:49.730
We used to play tag and stuff.

460
00:23:49.730 --> 00:23:51.440
Cool kids whispering at three o'clock!

461
00:23:51.560 --> 00:23:52.650
- Did you see that look?  - No.

462
00:23:52.650 --> 00:23:53.990
They're judging us!

463
00:23:54.990 --> 00:23:57.570
Somebody help me! Grab that... everybody put...

464
00:23:57.570 --> 00:24:01.660
But everything's different now. Since we moved.

465
00:24:04.250 --> 00:24:07.260
No! We're crying! At school!

466
00:24:08.210 --> 00:24:10.760
What? Sadness! What are you doing?

467
00:24:11.380 --> 00:24:13.600
Oh, no! I'm sorry!

468
00:24:15.500 --> 00:24:16.840
It's a Core Memory!

469
00:24:16.840 --> 00:24:18.590
But it's blue.

470
00:24:20.180 --> 00:24:23.940
No! Wait! Stop it! No! No!

471
00:24:30.810 --> 00:24:32.020
Joy, no.

472
00:24:32.140 --> 00:24:33.520
That's a Core Memory!

473
00:24:33.520 --> 00:24:35.360
- Joy, wait!  - Stop it! Let go!

474
00:24:35.360 --> 00:24:37.210
The Core Memories!

475
00:24:51.920 --> 00:24:53.470
No, no, no, no!

476
00:25:06.680 --> 00:25:07.890
Thank you, Riley.

477
00:25:07.890 --> 00:25:10.480
I know it can be tough moving to a new place,

478
00:25:10.480 --> 00:25:13.020
but we're happy to have you here.

479
00:25:13.020 --> 00:25:15.190
All right, everyone, get out your history books

480
00:25:15.190 --> 00:25:17.320
and turn to chapter seven.

481
00:25:19.400 --> 00:25:21.420
Can I say that curse word now?

482
00:25:42.340 --> 00:25:45.570
No! One, two, three. Okay.

483
00:25:46.600 --> 00:25:48.020
I got them.

484
00:25:48.890 --> 00:25:50.350
Where are we?

485
00:25:51.020 --> 00:25:53.900
Long Term Memory? Wait...

486
00:25:59.810 --> 00:26:01.910
Goofball Island?

487
00:26:02.440 --> 00:26:06.790
Riley's Islands of Personality. They're all down!

488
00:26:07.700 --> 00:26:09.120
This is bad.

489
00:26:09.120 --> 00:26:11.620
We...we can fix this!

490
00:26:11.620 --> 00:26:13.540
We just have to get back to Headquarters,

491
00:26:13.540 --> 00:26:15.160
plug the Core Memories in,

492
00:26:15.160 --> 00:26:17.250
and Riley will be back to normal.

493
00:26:18.130 --> 00:26:20.330
Riley has no Core Memories.

494
00:26:20.330 --> 00:26:23.300
No Personality Islands and no...

495
00:26:23.510 --> 00:26:24.760
What? What is it?

496
00:26:24.760 --> 00:26:25.800
You.

497
00:26:25.800 --> 00:26:27.970
You're not in headquarters.

498
00:26:27.970 --> 00:26:30.430
Without you, Riley can't be happy.

499
00:26:31.270 --> 00:26:32.950
We got to get you back up there.

500
00:26:33.520 --> 00:26:34.990
I'm coming, Riley.

501
00:26:49.040 --> 00:26:50.370
So, as it turns out,

502
00:26:50.370 --> 00:26:52.490
the green trash can is not recycling,

503
00:26:52.490 --> 00:26:55.130
it's for greens. Like compost. And eggshells.

504
00:26:55.130 --> 00:26:56.710
And the blue one is recycling.

505
00:26:56.710 --> 00:26:57.760
And the black one is trash.

506
00:26:57.770 --> 00:26:58.920
Riley is acting so weird.

507
00:26:58.920 --> 00:26:59.960
Why is she acting so weird?

508
00:26:59.960 --> 00:27:02.380
What do you expect? All the islands are down.

509
00:27:02.380 --> 00:27:03.590
Joy would know what to do.

510
00:27:03.590 --> 00:27:04.720
That's it.

511
00:27:04.720 --> 00:27:07.640
Until she gets back, we just do what Joy would do!

512
00:27:07.640 --> 00:27:08.510
Great idea.

513
00:27:08.510 --> 00:27:10.470
Anger, Fear, Disgust,

514
00:27:10.470 --> 00:27:12.430
how are we supposed to be happy?

515
00:27:12.430 --> 00:27:14.200
Hey, Riley. I've got good news!

516
00:27:14.640 --> 00:27:17.480
I found a junior hockey league right here in San Francisco.

517
00:27:17.480 --> 00:27:18.420
And get this,

518
00:27:18.420 --> 00:27:20.390
Try-outs are tomorrow after school.

519
00:27:20.390 --> 00:27:21.530
What luck, right?

520
00:27:21.530 --> 00:27:23.030
- Hockey?  - What do we do?

521
00:27:23.030 --> 00:27:24.570
Guys, this is...

522
00:27:24.570 --> 00:27:25.950
You pretend to be Joy.

523
00:27:25.950 --> 00:27:28.530
Won't it be great to be back out on the ice?

524
00:27:29.910 --> 00:27:32.130
Yeah, that sounds fantastic.

525
00:27:32.870 --> 00:27:35.000
What was that? That wasn't anything like Joy!

526
00:27:35.000 --> 00:27:37.300
- Because I'm not Joy.  - Yeah, no kidding.

527
00:27:39.340 --> 00:27:40.710
Did you guys pick up on that?

528
00:27:40.710 --> 00:27:42.710
- Something's wrong.  - Totally.

529
00:27:42.710 --> 00:27:44.010
Should we ask her?

530
00:27:44.010 --> 00:27:44.680
Let's probe.

531
00:27:44.680 --> 00:27:46.880
But keep it subtle, so she doesn't notice.

532
00:27:46.880 --> 00:27:49.220
So, how was the first day of school?

533
00:27:49.220 --> 00:27:50.430
She's probing us.

534
00:27:50.430 --> 00:27:51.970
I'm done. You pretend to be Joy.

535
00:27:51.970 --> 00:27:53.730
What? Okay.

536
00:27:54.520 --> 00:27:57.730
It was fine, I guess. I don't know.

537
00:27:57.730 --> 00:28:00.560
Very smooth. That was just like Joy.

538
00:28:00.560 --> 00:28:02.730
Something is definitely going on.

539
00:28:02.730 --> 00:28:05.190
She's never acted like this before. What should we do?

540
00:28:05.190 --> 00:28:06.900
We're going to find out what's happening.

541
00:28:06.900 --> 00:28:08.240
But we'll need support.

542
00:28:08.240 --> 00:28:09.330
Signal the husband.

543
00:28:13.120 --> 00:28:15.030
With a nice pass over to Reeves,

544
00:28:15.030 --> 00:28:16.660
comes across...And nice!

545
00:28:20.130 --> 00:28:21.260
She's looking at us.

546
00:28:22.840 --> 00:28:24.420
- What did she say?  - What?

547
00:28:24.420 --> 00:28:25.920
Sorry, sir. No one was listening.

548
00:28:25.920 --> 00:28:28.380
Is it garbage night? We left the toilet seat up?

549
00:28:28.380 --> 00:28:30.260
What? What is it, woman? What?

550
00:28:30.260 --> 00:28:32.510
He's making that stupid face again.

551
00:28:32.510 --> 00:28:34.430
I could strangle him right now.

552
00:28:34.430 --> 00:28:35.680
Signal him again.

553
00:28:39.190 --> 00:28:41.110
So, Riley, how was school?

554
00:28:41.110 --> 00:28:43.070
- You got to be kidding me!  - Seriously?

555
00:28:43.070 --> 00:28:44.490
For this we gave up that

556
00:28:44.490 --> 00:28:46.330
Brazilian helicopter pilot?

557
00:28:46.570 --> 00:28:48.280
Move! I'll be Joy.

558
00:28:48.280 --> 00:28:50.200
School was great, all right?

559
00:28:50.200 --> 00:28:52.380
Riley. Is everything okay?

560
00:28:53.700 --> 00:28:55.450
Sir, she just rolled her eyes at us.

561
00:28:55.450 --> 00:28:57.120
What is her deal?

562
00:28:57.120 --> 00:28:58.870
All right, make a show of force.

563
00:28:58.870 --> 00:29:00.460
I don't want to have to put the foot Down.

564
00:29:00.460 --> 00:29:02.460
No, not the foot!

565
00:29:02.460 --> 00:29:04.800
Riley, I do not like this new attitude.

566
00:29:04.800 --> 00:29:06.500
I'll show you attitude, old man.

567
00:29:06.500 --> 00:29:07.800
No. No, no, no! Stay happy!

568
00:29:08.550 --> 00:29:10.930
What is your problem? Just leave me alone!

569
00:29:10.930 --> 00:29:12.720
Sir, reporting high levels of sass!

570
00:29:12.720 --> 00:29:14.640
Take it to defcon two.

571
00:29:14.640 --> 00:29:16.690
You heard that, gentlemen. Defcon two.

572
00:29:17.990 --> 00:29:18.750
Listen, young lady,

573
00:29:18.750 --> 00:29:21.650
I don't know where this disrespectful attitude came from...

574
00:29:21.650 --> 00:29:24.570
You want a piece of this, pops? Come and get it!

575
00:29:24.570 --> 00:29:26.150
Yeah, well... well...

576
00:29:26.150 --> 00:29:28.530
Here it comes. Prepare the foot!

577
00:29:29.990 --> 00:29:31.500
Keys to safety position.

578
00:29:33.320 --> 00:29:34.910
Ready to launch on your command, sir!

579
00:29:37.580 --> 00:29:39.220
Just shut up!

580
00:29:40.160 --> 00:29:41.830
Fire!

581
00:29:41.830 --> 00:29:45.710
That's it! Go to your room! Now!

582
00:29:48.840 --> 00:29:51.850
The foot is down! The foot is down!

583
00:29:53.010 --> 00:29:56.850
Good job, gentlemen. That could have been a disaster.

584
00:29:57.260 --> 00:29:58.930
Well, that was a disaster.

585
00:30:02.100 --> 00:30:04.820
Come fly with me, Gatinha.

586
00:30:17.200 --> 00:30:19.950
We're going to walk out there? On that?

587
00:30:19.950 --> 00:30:21.790
It's the quickest way back.

588
00:30:21.790 --> 00:30:23.920
But it's right over the Memory Dump.

589
00:30:23.920 --> 00:30:26.310
If we fall, we'll be forgotten forever.

590
00:30:26.500 --> 00:30:28.390
We have to do this for Riley.

591
00:30:28.390 --> 00:30:30.770
- Just follow my footsteps.  - Okay.

592
00:30:30.770 --> 00:30:34.850
It's not that high. It's totally fine...

593
00:30:52.070 --> 00:30:55.130
So, things got a little out of hand downstairs.

594
00:30:56.070 --> 00:30:57.990
Do you want to talk about it?

595
00:30:59.040 --> 00:31:01.340
Come on, where's my happy girl?

596
00:31:02.750 --> 00:31:03.880
Monkey.

597
00:31:04.830 --> 00:31:06.840
He's trying to start up Goofball.

598
00:31:08.070 --> 00:31:09.360
Come on!

599
00:31:21.750 --> 00:31:23.340
Go back! Run, run, run!

600
00:31:51.110 --> 00:31:52.490
What...

601
00:32:07.750 --> 00:32:10.590
I get it. You need some alone time.

602
00:32:13.510 --> 00:32:14.850
We'll talk later.

603
00:32:18.310 --> 00:32:20.150
We have a Major problem.

604
00:32:20.730 --> 00:32:22.240
Joy, where are you?

605
00:32:23.440 --> 00:32:25.980
We lost Goofball Island.

606
00:32:25.980 --> 00:32:27.570
That means she can lose

607
00:32:27.580 --> 00:32:30.780
friendship and hockey and honesty and family.

608
00:32:30.780 --> 00:32:33.400
You can fix this, right, Joy?

609
00:32:33.410 --> 00:32:34.500
I...

610
00:32:35.700 --> 00:32:37.070
I don't know.

611
00:32:37.080 --> 00:32:39.260
But we have to try. Okay, come on.

612
00:32:40.540 --> 00:32:42.620
Riley's gone to sleep.

613
00:32:42.620 --> 00:32:46.710
Which is a good thing. When you think about it because

614
00:32:46.710 --> 00:32:48.960
nothing else bad can happen while she's asleep.

615
00:32:48.960 --> 00:32:51.130
We'll be back to headquarters before she wakes up.

616
00:32:51.130 --> 00:32:53.760
We'll just go across Friendship Island.

617
00:32:55.800 --> 00:32:57.550
We'll never make it.

618
00:32:57.550 --> 00:32:58.890
No! No, no, no!

619
00:32:58.890 --> 00:33:00.350
Don't obsess over the weight of life's problems.

620
00:33:00.350 --> 00:33:02.220
Remember the funny movie where the dog dies?

621
00:33:02.230 --> 00:33:04.810
Sadness, we don't have time for this.

622
00:33:04.810 --> 00:33:08.400
We'll just have to go around. Take the scenic route.

623
00:33:08.400 --> 00:33:10.860
Wait, Joy, you could get lost in there!

624
00:33:10.860 --> 00:33:12.480
Think positive!

625
00:33:12.490 --> 00:33:16.130
Okay. I'm positive you will get lost in there.

626
00:33:16.660 --> 00:33:18.410
That's long term memory.

627
00:33:18.410 --> 00:33:21.040
An endless Warren of corridors and shelves.

628
00:33:21.040 --> 00:33:23.580
I read about it in the manuals.

629
00:33:23.580 --> 00:33:26.620
The manuals? The manuals!

630
00:33:26.630 --> 00:33:28.540
- You read the manuals!  - Yeah.

631
00:33:28.540 --> 00:33:30.750
So you know the way back to headquarters!

632
00:33:30.750 --> 00:33:31.840
I guess.

633
00:33:34.880 --> 00:33:36.010
You are my map!

634
00:33:36.430 --> 00:33:39.720
Let's go! Lead on, my map! Show me where we're going!

635
00:33:39.720 --> 00:33:43.520
Okay. Only I'm too sad to walk.

636
00:33:43.520 --> 00:33:46.620
Just give me a few...Hours.

637
00:33:48.060 --> 00:33:49.270
Which way? Left?

638
00:33:49.270 --> 00:33:50.480
Right.

639
00:33:50.980 --> 00:33:54.490
No. I mean, go left. I said left was right. Like "Correct."

640
00:33:54.490 --> 00:33:55.740
Okay.

641
00:33:55.740 --> 00:33:57.950
This actually feels kind of nice.

642
00:33:57.950 --> 00:33:59.060
Okay, here we go!

643
00:33:59.060 --> 00:34:01.370
We'll be back to headquarters before morning.

644
00:34:01.370 --> 00:34:05.050
We can do it! This will be easy! This is working!

645
00:34:08.460 --> 00:34:11.290
This is not working. Are we getting close?

646
00:34:11.290 --> 00:34:12.880
Yeah, just another right.

647
00:34:13.460 --> 00:34:18.470
And...A left and then another...Left and...

648
00:34:18.470 --> 00:34:20.930
Are you sure you know where we're going?

649
00:34:20.930 --> 00:34:23.780
Because we seem to be walking away from headquarters.

650
00:34:24.560 --> 00:34:26.450
Riley's awake.

651
00:34:30.520 --> 00:34:32.060
Don't touch. Remember?

652
00:34:32.060 --> 00:34:34.650
If you touch them, they stay sad.

653
00:34:34.650 --> 00:34:38.200
Sorry, I won't. Starting now.

654
00:34:38.200 --> 00:34:40.570
I can't take much more of this.

655
00:34:40.570 --> 00:34:42.160
Forget them!

656
00:34:42.160 --> 00:34:44.760
- Mind workers!  - But, Joy, we're almost...

657
00:34:45.870 --> 00:34:48.750
Phone numbers. We don't need all these. They're in her phone.

658
00:34:48.750 --> 00:34:50.890
- Excuse me, hi.  - Just forget all of that. Please. Forget it!

659
00:34:52.340 --> 00:34:54.000
- I need to find Friendship Island.  - Look at this.

660
00:34:54.000 --> 00:34:55.500
Four years of piano lessons.

661
00:34:55.510 --> 00:34:56.840
Yeah, it looks pretty faded.

662
00:34:56.840 --> 00:34:58.670
You know what? Save Chopsticks and Heart and Soul,

663
00:34:58.670 --> 00:34:59.800
get rid of the rest.

664
00:35:00.300 --> 00:35:02.010
- Are you...  - U.S. Presidents. What do you think?

665
00:35:02.010 --> 00:35:04.260
Yeah, just keep Washington, Lincoln and the fat one.

666
00:35:04.260 --> 00:35:06.520
- Forget 'em!  - Hey! You can't throw those away!

667
00:35:06.520 --> 00:35:07.930
Those are perfectly good memories.

668
00:35:07.930 --> 00:35:10.270
The names of every "Cutie Pie Princess" Doll?

669
00:35:10.270 --> 00:35:11.880
Yes! That is critical information!

670
00:35:11.880 --> 00:35:13.440
Glitterstorm, Honeypants...

671
00:35:13.440 --> 00:35:14.780
Forget 'em!

672
00:35:19.450 --> 00:35:20.740
Hey! Bring those back!

673
00:35:20.740 --> 00:35:23.030
They're in the dump. Nothing comes back from the dump.

674
00:35:23.030 --> 00:35:24.700
Yeah. Look, lady, this is our job, okay?

675
00:35:24.700 --> 00:35:27.160
When Riley doesn't care about a memory, it fades.

676
00:35:27.160 --> 00:35:28.580
- Fades?  - Happens to the best of them.

677
00:35:28.580 --> 00:35:32.460
Yeah, except for this bad boy. This one will never fade.

678
00:35:32.670 --> 00:35:34.630
- Tripledent gum  - Will make you smile

679
00:35:34.630 --> 00:35:36.000
The song from the gum commercial?

680
00:35:36.000 --> 00:35:36.950
You know, sometimes we send

681
00:35:36.950 --> 00:35:38.510
that one up to headquarters for no reason.

682
00:35:38.510 --> 00:35:40.970
It just plays in Riley's head over and over again.

683
00:35:40.970 --> 00:35:42.800
Like a million times!

684
00:35:42.800 --> 00:35:43.930
Let's watch it again!

685
00:35:43.930 --> 00:35:45.550
Tripledent gum

686
00:35:45.560 --> 00:35:47.170
Yeah, I know. We all know the song.

687
00:35:47.170 --> 00:35:48.600
Okay. Yeah, real catchy. Okay.

688
00:35:48.600 --> 00:35:49.850
Hey, what do you think? Should we do it?

689
00:35:49.850 --> 00:35:50.890
Yeah!

690
00:35:50.890 --> 00:35:52.480
Okay, here we go!

691
00:35:55.570 --> 00:35:56.730
Tripledent gum

692
00:35:56.730 --> 00:35:58.490
What the... this again?

693
00:35:59.740 --> 00:36:02.170
Wait! Do you know how to get to Friendship Island?

694
00:36:02.410 --> 00:36:03.490
Tripledent gum

695
00:36:03.490 --> 00:36:04.450
Do you like it there?

696
00:36:04.450 --> 00:36:06.740
Did you feel any earthquakes? Is the bridge cool?

697
00:36:06.740 --> 00:36:09.580
Yeah, it's good. What happened with the playoffs?

698
00:36:09.580 --> 00:36:10.660
We won the first game.

699
00:36:10.660 --> 00:36:12.960
Coach says we might actually go to the finals this year.

700
00:36:12.960 --> 00:36:15.920
And we've got this new girl on the team. She's so cool.

701
00:36:15.920 --> 00:36:17.500
She did not just say that.

702
00:36:17.500 --> 00:36:20.380
A new girl? Meg has a new friend already?

703
00:36:20.760 --> 00:36:22.050
Hey, hey! Stay happy!

704
00:36:22.050 --> 00:36:24.180
We do not want to lose any more islands here, guys!

705
00:36:24.390 --> 00:36:26.550
We can pass the puck to each other without even looking.

706
00:36:26.560 --> 00:36:28.010
It's like mind reading!

707
00:36:28.010 --> 00:36:29.390
You like to read minds, Meg?

708
00:36:29.390 --> 00:36:31.310
I got something for you to read, right here!

709
00:36:31.310 --> 00:36:32.730
Let's just be calm for one second!

710
00:36:33.560 --> 00:36:35.190
- I heard they have parrots...  - I've got to go.

711
00:36:35.190 --> 00:36:36.660
- What?  - I got to go!

712
00:36:37.940 --> 00:36:42.240
Okay, could you just please tell me which way is... oh, no!

713
00:36:45.700 --> 00:36:47.840
Friendship Island! What?

714
00:36:59.000 --> 00:37:00.420
Not friendship.

715
00:37:06.800 --> 00:37:10.850
Riley loved that one. And now it's gone.

716
00:37:10.850 --> 00:37:14.570
Goodbye, friendship. Hello, loneliness.

717
00:37:18.900 --> 00:37:20.910
We'll just have to go the long way.

718
00:37:21.650 --> 00:37:26.120
Yeah. The long, long, long, long way.

719
00:37:26.990 --> 00:37:28.410
I'm ready.

720
00:37:29.620 --> 00:37:31.970
There's got to be a better way.

721
00:37:34.410 --> 00:37:35.580
Look at you!

722
00:37:36.880 --> 00:37:39.500
I will take you, but not you.

723
00:37:39.500 --> 00:37:41.630
Who am I kidding? I can't leave you.

724
00:37:41.960 --> 00:37:43.840
Hello!

725
00:37:43.840 --> 00:37:45.140
Wait! Hey! Wait!

726
00:37:47.430 --> 00:37:49.110
Wait! Stop!

727
00:37:57.770 --> 00:37:58.900
Excuse me.

728
00:37:59.560 --> 00:38:02.440
- I was looking for...  - Diversion!

729
00:38:02.440 --> 00:38:04.400
- What?  - So long, sucker!

730
00:38:05.950 --> 00:38:07.110
I hurt all over.

731
00:38:07.110 --> 00:38:08.990
Wait. I know you.

732
00:38:08.990 --> 00:38:11.180
No, you don't. I get that a lot.

733
00:38:11.180 --> 00:38:12.620
I look like a lot of people.

734
00:38:12.620 --> 00:38:14.080
No, no, no. I do.

735
00:38:14.080 --> 00:38:16.870
Bing Bong! Riley's imaginary friend!

736
00:38:16.870 --> 00:38:19.420
- You really do know me?  - Well, of course!

737
00:38:19.420 --> 00:38:20.900
Riley loved playing with you!

738
00:38:20.910 --> 00:38:22.040
You two are best friends!

739
00:38:22.050 --> 00:38:24.590
You would know. We're trying to get back to headquarters.

740
00:38:24.590 --> 00:38:26.840
Headquarters? You guys are from headquarters?

741
00:38:26.840 --> 00:38:30.010
Well, yeah. I'm Joy. This is Sadness.

742
00:38:30.010 --> 00:38:31.760
You're Joy? The Joy?

743
00:38:31.760 --> 00:38:33.430
What the heck are you doing out here?

744
00:38:33.430 --> 00:38:35.600
That's a good question. You want to answer that, Sadness?

745
00:38:35.600 --> 00:38:38.640
Without you, Riley won't ever be happy.

746
00:38:38.650 --> 00:38:41.110
We can't have that. We got to get you back.

747
00:38:41.110 --> 00:38:43.190
I'll tell you what. Follow me!

748
00:38:43.190 --> 00:38:44.280
Thank you!

749
00:38:44.280 --> 00:38:45.990
It is so great to see you again.

750
00:38:45.990 --> 00:38:48.280
I gotta tell you, I am such a huge fan of your work.

751
00:38:48.280 --> 00:38:51.370
Do you remember when you and Riley were in a band?

752
00:38:51.370 --> 00:38:53.280
I went to all of your concerts.

753
00:38:53.290 --> 00:38:54.790
Yeah, I blow a mean nose.

754
00:38:54.790 --> 00:38:56.410
Watching you play tag was such a treat.

755
00:38:56.410 --> 00:38:57.790
Two-time world champ.

756
00:38:57.790 --> 00:38:59.500
And remember your rockets?

757
00:38:59.500 --> 00:39:01.830
Of course! It runs on song power!

758
00:39:01.840 --> 00:39:03.340
That's right! Your theme song!

759
00:39:03.340 --> 00:39:04.800
Who's your friend who likes to play?*

760
00:39:04.800 --> 00:39:06.130
Bing bong bing bong

761
00:39:06.130 --> 00:39:07.550
His rocket makes you yell "Hooray!"

762
00:39:07.550 --> 00:39:09.340
- Bing bong, bing bong  - Bing bong, bing bong

763
00:39:09.340 --> 00:39:11.760
What exactly are you supposed to be?

764
00:39:11.760 --> 00:39:14.560
You know, it's unclear. I'm mostly cotton candy.

765
00:39:14.560 --> 00:39:19.350
But shape-wise I'm part cat, part elephant, part dolphin.

766
00:39:19.350 --> 00:39:20.310
Dolphin?

767
00:39:23.320 --> 00:39:25.140
You got to remember, when Riley was three,

768
00:39:25.140 --> 00:39:26.360
animals were all the rage.

769
00:39:26.360 --> 00:39:28.320
The cow goes moo. The horse goes neigh.

770
00:39:28.320 --> 00:39:30.030
That's all people talked about back then.

771
00:39:30.030 --> 00:39:32.620
Yeah. Yeah. I guess that's true. What are you doing out here?

772
00:39:32.620 --> 00:39:36.120
Well, there's not much call for imaginary friends lately.

773
00:39:36.120 --> 00:39:38.670
So I, you know...

774
00:39:40.290 --> 00:39:42.710
Hey, hey. Don't be sad.

775
00:39:42.710 --> 00:39:44.880
Tell you what. When I get back up to headquarters,

776
00:39:44.880 --> 00:39:46.920
I'll make sure Riley remembers you.

777
00:39:46.920 --> 00:39:49.340
- You will?  - Of course! She'd love that.

778
00:39:50.380 --> 00:39:52.930
This is the greatest day of my life!

779
00:39:56.770 --> 00:39:57.860
Are you okay?

780
00:39:58.980 --> 00:40:01.310
- Hey, what's going on?  - I cry candy.

781
00:40:01.310 --> 00:40:03.520
Try the caramel. It's delicious.

782
00:40:05.570 --> 00:40:07.150
- Here, use this.  - Thanks!

783
00:40:07.150 --> 00:40:08.280
Hold on, wait a second.

784
00:40:11.740 --> 00:40:13.880
It always gets stuck at the bottom.

785
00:40:16.450 --> 00:40:19.580
Here. What? It's imaginary.

786
00:40:19.580 --> 00:40:20.700
Thanks. This will make it

787
00:40:20.700 --> 00:40:22.670
a lot easier to walk back to headquarters.

788
00:40:22.670 --> 00:40:24.500
Walk? We're not walking.

789
00:40:24.500 --> 00:40:26.670
We're taking the train of thought!

790
00:40:27.920 --> 00:40:30.130
The train, of course!

791
00:40:30.130 --> 00:40:32.720
That is so much faster! But how do we catch it?

792
00:40:32.720 --> 00:40:34.510
Well, it kind of goes all over the place,

793
00:40:34.510 --> 00:40:36.970
but there is a station in Imagination Land.

794
00:40:36.970 --> 00:40:39.720
I know a shortcut. Come on, this way!

795
00:40:39.720 --> 00:40:41.980
I am so glad we ran into you!

796
00:40:42.520 --> 00:40:45.270
The station is right through here. After you.

797
00:40:45.270 --> 00:40:46.690
- Joy.  - What?

798
00:40:46.690 --> 00:40:48.500
I read about this place in the manual.

799
00:40:48.500 --> 00:40:49.900
We shouldn't go in there.

800
00:40:49.900 --> 00:40:52.490
Bing bong says it's the quickest way to headquarters.

801
00:40:52.490 --> 00:40:54.740
No, but, Joy, this is abstract thought.

802
00:40:54.740 --> 00:40:56.050
What are you talking about?

803
00:40:56.050 --> 00:40:58.370
I go in here all the time. It's a shortcut, you see?

804
00:40:58.370 --> 00:41:02.950
D-a-n-g-e-r. Shortcut. I'll prove it to you.

805
00:41:03.540 --> 00:41:05.830
Look at me. I'm closer to the station

806
00:41:05.830 --> 00:41:08.210
because I'm taking the shortcut.

807
00:41:08.960 --> 00:41:10.460
Let's go around. This way.

808
00:41:10.460 --> 00:41:12.300
Almost there!

809
00:41:13.090 --> 00:41:15.720
If you want to walk the long way, go for it.

810
00:41:15.720 --> 00:41:17.760
But Riley needs to be happy.

811
00:41:17.760 --> 00:41:18.790
I'm not missing that train.

812
00:41:18.790 --> 00:41:20.600
Bing bong knows what he's doing.

813
00:41:20.600 --> 00:41:22.560
He's part dolphin. They're very smart.

814
00:41:22.560 --> 00:41:24.320
Well, I guess.

815
00:41:27.440 --> 00:41:29.290
- What did you get?  - I don't know.

816
00:41:43.120 --> 00:41:46.500
Okay, what abstract concept are we trying to comprehend today?

817
00:41:47.080 --> 00:41:48.830
Loneliness.

818
00:41:48.840 --> 00:41:50.460
Looks like there's something in there.

819
00:41:50.460 --> 00:41:52.960
I'm going to turn it on for a minute and burn out the gunk.

820
00:41:52.960 --> 00:41:55.590
What did I tell you? You'll be at headquarters in no time.

821
00:41:56.590 --> 00:41:58.260
Hey, would you look at that?

822
00:41:59.850 --> 00:42:02.030
- What's happening?  - Oh, no, they turned it on.

823
00:42:02.720 --> 00:42:03.980
Never seen this before.

824
00:42:06.730 --> 00:42:09.700
My face! My beautiful face!

825
00:42:10.400 --> 00:42:11.860
- What is going on?  - We're abstracting!

826
00:42:11.860 --> 00:42:13.160
There are four stages.

827
00:42:13.160 --> 00:42:16.030
This is the first: Non-objective fragmentation!

828
00:42:16.030 --> 00:42:17.200
All right. Do not panic.

829
00:42:17.200 --> 00:42:19.710
What is important is that we all stay together.

830
00:42:21.120 --> 00:42:23.740
We're in the second stage. We're deconstructing!

831
00:42:23.750 --> 00:42:24.840
Run!

832
00:42:26.620 --> 00:42:28.090
I can't feel my legs!

833
00:42:28.710 --> 00:42:29.920
There they are.

834
00:42:29.920 --> 00:42:31.220
Come here, me!

835
00:42:32.800 --> 00:42:34.150
We've got to get out of here

836
00:42:34.150 --> 00:42:36.920
before we're nothing but shape and color!

837
00:42:36.930 --> 00:42:38.510
We'll get stuck here forever!

838
00:42:38.510 --> 00:42:40.340
Stuck? Why did we come in here?

839
00:42:40.350 --> 00:42:43.010
I told you, it's a shortcut!

840
00:42:43.010 --> 00:42:44.690
The train!

841
00:42:48.350 --> 00:42:52.150
Oh, no. We're two-dimensional! That's stage three!

842
00:42:52.150 --> 00:42:53.190
We're getting nowhere!

843
00:42:53.190 --> 00:42:56.360
- Depth! I'm lacking depth!  - Come on.

844
00:42:59.410 --> 00:43:00.740
We can't fit.

845
00:43:00.740 --> 00:43:04.660
Oh, no, we're nonfigurative. This is the last stage!

846
00:43:04.660 --> 00:43:06.500
We're not going to make it!

847
00:43:08.330 --> 00:43:11.960
Wait! We're two-dimensional. Fall on your face!

848
00:43:22.720 --> 00:43:24.730
Stop! Stop!

849
00:43:25.930 --> 00:43:29.140
No! I thought you said that was a shortcut.

850
00:43:29.140 --> 00:43:32.150
I did, but wow, we should not have gone in there.

851
00:43:32.150 --> 00:43:34.120
That was dangerous! They really should put up a sign.

852
00:43:34.360 --> 00:43:35.450
How long until the next train?

853
00:43:35.570 --> 00:43:39.320
Who knows. But don't worry. There's another station. That way.

854
00:43:39.320 --> 00:43:40.670
The train always stops there.

855
00:43:40.680 --> 00:43:42.490
Right before it goes to headquarters.

856
00:43:42.490 --> 00:43:44.530
If we hurry, we can catch it.

857
00:43:44.530 --> 00:43:46.910
This isn't another one of your shortcuts, is it?

858
00:43:47.750 --> 00:43:49.370
Yeah!

859
00:43:49.370 --> 00:43:51.210
Is there really another station?

860
00:43:51.210 --> 00:43:52.470
Through there.

861
00:43:54.590 --> 00:43:57.180
Welcome to Imagination Land!

862
00:43:57.380 --> 00:43:59.510
- Imagination land?  - Sure!

863
00:43:59.510 --> 00:44:01.930
I come here all the time. I'm practically the mayor.

864
00:44:01.930 --> 00:44:04.760
Hey, you guys hungry? There's French Fry Forest!

865
00:44:04.760 --> 00:44:07.100
- Delicious.  - No way!

866
00:44:07.100 --> 00:44:09.810
Check it out! Trophy Town!

867
00:44:09.810 --> 00:44:12.980
Medals! Ribbons! Everyone's a winner!

868
00:44:13.650 --> 00:44:15.690
I won first place!

869
00:44:15.690 --> 00:44:18.530
- Me too!  - Participation award.

870
00:44:18.530 --> 00:44:22.030
Wait, is that... Sadness, look, it's Cloud Town!

871
00:44:22.030 --> 00:44:24.070
That is my favorite!

872
00:44:24.070 --> 00:44:25.530
It's so soft!

873
00:44:25.530 --> 00:44:27.330
Let me try.

874
00:44:27.330 --> 00:44:29.200
Hey! What's the big idea?

875
00:44:29.200 --> 00:44:32.000
You better fix that wall, or else you're in big troub...

876
00:44:34.040 --> 00:44:35.500
Oh, no! Lava!

877
00:44:36.920 --> 00:44:38.920
Imagination Land is the best!

878
00:44:40.050 --> 00:44:42.880
Is it all going to be so interactive?

879
00:44:42.880 --> 00:44:45.260
Hey, look! The House of Cards!

880
00:44:45.260 --> 00:44:47.680
Wait. Hang on just a minute.

881
00:44:47.680 --> 00:44:49.220
- Your rocket!  - Yeah.

882
00:44:49.220 --> 00:44:51.020
I stashed it in there for safekeeping,

883
00:44:51.020 --> 00:44:53.530
and now I'm all set to take Riley to the moon!

884
00:44:54.650 --> 00:44:56.520
- I'm sorry.  - Great.

885
00:44:56.520 --> 00:44:58.690
I love Imagination Land.

886
00:44:58.690 --> 00:45:01.530
Isn't it great? And there's always something new, like...

887
00:45:03.950 --> 00:45:05.360
Who the heck is that?

888
00:45:05.370 --> 00:45:06.780
Imaginary boyfriend.

889
00:45:06.780 --> 00:45:08.700
I would die for Riley.

890
00:45:09.450 --> 00:45:11.670
- I've never seen him before.  - I live in Canada.

891
00:45:12.410 --> 00:45:14.870
Anyway, this way. Through Preschool World!

892
00:45:14.880 --> 00:45:16.000
We're nearly to the train!

893
00:45:16.700 --> 00:45:18.170
Riley, here we come!

894
00:45:20.300 --> 00:45:23.880
This should be fun! New team, new friends.

895
00:45:23.880 --> 00:45:25.260
These kids look pretty good,

896
00:45:25.260 --> 00:45:26.970
considering they're from San Francisco.

897
00:45:26.970 --> 00:45:28.350
Okay, Andersen, you're up!

898
00:45:28.350 --> 00:45:31.470
- Got to go.  - Okay. Good luck, sweetie!

899
00:45:31.470 --> 00:45:32.730
Luck isn't going to help us now.

900
00:45:32.730 --> 00:45:34.560
If she tries to use Hockey Island, it's going down.

901
00:45:34.560 --> 00:45:37.980
Which is why I've recalled every hockey memory I can think of.

902
00:45:37.980 --> 00:45:40.820
One of these has got to work in place of the core memory.

903
00:45:40.820 --> 00:45:42.330
- She's about to play!  - Hurry!

904
00:45:49.990 --> 00:45:52.620
We did it, gang! It's working!

905
00:45:55.580 --> 00:45:59.920
Line change! Line change! Change it up!

906
00:46:04.720 --> 00:46:06.110
No! No!

907
00:46:11.470 --> 00:46:13.310
It's like we don't learn anything.

908
00:46:13.310 --> 00:46:15.390
- Come on!  - Let's pick it up out there!

909
00:46:15.390 --> 00:46:17.940
Pass! Shoot it! Shoot it!

910
00:46:20.270 --> 00:46:21.900
- That's it!  - No, no, no! Breathe.

911
00:46:21.900 --> 00:46:23.200
Find your happy place.

912
00:46:27.490 --> 00:46:29.000
What's her problem?

913
00:46:35.290 --> 00:46:37.330
- Riley. What's wrong?  - Let's go.

914
00:46:37.330 --> 00:46:39.920
- You're not going to finish try-outs?  - What's the point?

915
00:46:39.920 --> 00:46:42.290
Hey. It'll be all right. Let's just go back...

916
00:46:42.300 --> 00:46:44.440
Stop saying everything will be all right!

917
00:46:46.510 --> 00:46:47.940
Nice hustle, ladies!

918
00:46:56.180 --> 00:46:57.310
Hockey?

919
00:47:00.400 --> 00:47:04.940
No, no, she loves hockey. She can't give up hockey.

920
00:47:04.940 --> 00:47:07.280
Hey! Look at that! Very nice shot!

921
00:47:07.280 --> 00:47:09.240
Bing Bong, we have to get to that station.

922
00:47:09.240 --> 00:47:11.450
Sure thing. This way, just past Graham Cracker Castle.

923
00:47:11.450 --> 00:47:14.700
Hey. That's weird. Graham Cracker Castle used to be right here.

924
00:47:14.700 --> 00:47:17.080
I wonder why they moved it? That's not...

925
00:47:17.080 --> 00:47:19.670
I would have sworn Sparkle Pony Mountain was right here.

926
00:47:19.670 --> 00:47:21.500
- Hey, what's going on?  - Yeah, yeah. I don't know...

927
00:47:21.500 --> 00:47:23.170
- We'll have to come back.  - Princess Dream World!

928
00:47:25.880 --> 00:47:29.010
Oh, no! The Stuffed Animal Hall of Fame!

929
00:47:30.510 --> 00:47:31.600
My rocket!

930
00:47:32.680 --> 00:47:34.510
Wait! Riley and I, we're still using that rocket!

931
00:47:34.510 --> 00:47:37.100
It still has some song power left!

932
00:47:37.100 --> 00:47:38.690
Who's your friend who likes to play?

933
00:47:44.940 --> 00:47:48.900
No! No, no, no. No, you can't take my rocket to the dump!

934
00:47:48.900 --> 00:47:50.280
Riley and I are going to the moon!

935
00:47:56.200 --> 00:47:58.370
Riley can't be done with me.

936
00:48:04.960 --> 00:48:08.130
Hey, it's going to be okay! We can fix this!

937
00:48:08.130 --> 00:48:10.130
We just need to get back to headquarters.

938
00:48:10.130 --> 00:48:11.510
Which way to the train station?

939
00:48:11.510 --> 00:48:14.100
I had a whole trip planned for us.

940
00:48:15.350 --> 00:48:20.070
Hey, who's ticklish, huh? Here comes the tickle monster!

941
00:48:21.390 --> 00:48:22.900
Hey, Bing Bong! Look at this!

942
00:48:25.820 --> 00:48:27.110
Here's a fun game!

943
00:48:27.110 --> 00:48:31.280
You point to the train station and we all go there!

944
00:48:31.280 --> 00:48:34.580
Won't that be fun? Come on, let's go to the train station!

945
00:48:36.160 --> 00:48:38.000
I'm sorry they took your rocket.

946
00:48:38.950 --> 00:48:41.370
They took something that you loved.

947
00:48:41.370 --> 00:48:43.500
It's gone. Forever.

948
00:48:43.500 --> 00:48:45.920
Sadness. Don't make him feel worse.

949
00:48:45.920 --> 00:48:46.700
Sorry.

950
00:48:46.700 --> 00:48:49.210
It's all I had left of Riley.

951
00:48:49.210 --> 00:48:51.970
I bet you and Riley had great adventures.

952
00:48:52.680 --> 00:48:54.180
They were wonderful.

953
00:48:54.180 --> 00:48:58.010
Once we flew back in time. We had breakfast twice that day.

954
00:48:58.010 --> 00:48:59.180
Sadness...

955
00:48:59.180 --> 00:49:01.900
It sounds amazing. I bet Riley liked it.

956
00:49:02.480 --> 00:49:06.610
She did. We were best friends.

957
00:49:06.610 --> 00:49:09.000
Yeah. It's sad.

958
00:49:21.200 --> 00:49:22.790
I'm okay now.

959
00:49:24.170 --> 00:49:27.100
Come on. The train station is this way.

960
00:49:33.510 --> 00:49:35.130
How did you do that?

961
00:49:35.140 --> 00:49:37.140
I don't know. He was sad.

962
00:49:37.140 --> 00:49:38.470
So I listened to what...

963
00:49:38.470 --> 00:49:40.980
Hey! There's the train!

964
00:49:51.280 --> 00:49:54.920
We made it! We're finally going to get home!

965
00:49:56.160 --> 00:49:59.660
Oh, no! These facts and opinions look so similar.

966
00:49:59.660 --> 00:50:02.330
Don't worry about it. Happens all the time.

967
00:50:06.670 --> 00:50:09.290
On a scale of one to ten, I give this day an F.

968
00:50:09.290 --> 00:50:12.420
Well, why don't we quit standing around and do something?

969
00:50:12.420 --> 00:50:13.590
Like what, genius?

970
00:50:13.590 --> 00:50:15.510
Like quitting. That's what I'm doing.

971
00:50:15.510 --> 00:50:19.690
Sure it's the coward's way out. But this coward's gonna survive.

972
00:50:27.350 --> 00:50:29.020
Emotions can't quit, genius!

973
00:50:30.770 --> 00:50:32.900
I thought we were supposed to be keeping Riley happy.

974
00:50:33.440 --> 00:50:35.070
Wait a minute! Wait a minute!

975
00:50:40.950 --> 00:50:42.580
- What is it?  - Nothing.

976
00:50:42.580 --> 00:50:44.950
- Just the best idea ever.  - What?

977
00:50:44.960 --> 00:50:47.620
All the good core memories were made in Minnesota.

978
00:50:47.620 --> 00:50:50.790
Ergo, we go back to Minnesota and make more.

979
00:50:50.790 --> 00:50:51.880
- Ta-da!  - Wait, wait, wait.

980
00:50:51.880 --> 00:50:53.880
You're saying we run away?

981
00:50:53.880 --> 00:50:55.340
Well, I wouldn't call it that.

982
00:50:55.340 --> 00:50:58.050
I'd call it the happy core memory development program.

983
00:50:58.050 --> 00:50:59.430
You can't be serious.

984
00:50:59.430 --> 00:51:00.930
Hey! Our life was perfect

985
00:51:00.930 --> 00:51:04.900
until mom and dad decided to move to San Fran stinktown.

986
00:51:05.560 --> 00:51:07.270
I mean, it's just so drastic!

987
00:51:07.270 --> 00:51:09.520
Need I remind you of how great things were there?

988
00:51:09.520 --> 00:51:12.280
Our room? Our back yard? Our friends?

989
00:51:13.980 --> 00:51:15.400
TripleDent Gum will make you smile.

990
00:51:15.400 --> 00:51:17.740
Did I ask for the gum commercial?

991
00:51:18.150 --> 00:51:19.660
Anyway, it was better, that's my point.

992
00:51:19.660 --> 00:51:22.240
Yeah, Riley was happier in Minnesota.

993
00:51:22.240 --> 00:51:24.410
Wait. Hold on. Shouldn't we just sleep on this or something?

994
00:51:24.830 --> 00:51:26.370
Fine. Let's sleep on it.

995
00:51:26.370 --> 00:51:29.330
Because, hey, I'm sure jolly fun-filled times

996
00:51:29.330 --> 00:51:31.800
are just around the corner.

997
00:51:43.720 --> 00:51:45.390
Hey, hey! Why aren't we moving?

998
00:51:45.390 --> 00:51:47.850
Riley's gone to sleep. We're all on break.

999
00:51:47.850 --> 00:51:49.730
You mean we're stuck here until morning?

1000
00:51:49.730 --> 00:51:52.020
Yeah, the train of thought doesn't run while she's asleep.

1001
00:51:52.020 --> 00:51:54.480
- We can't wait that long.  - How about we wake her up?

1002
00:51:54.480 --> 00:51:57.360
Sadness, that's ridiculous! How could we possibly...

1003
00:51:59.700 --> 00:52:00.820
How about we wake her up?

1004
00:52:00.820 --> 00:52:03.450
- Great idea, Joy.  - Thanks. Come on!

1005
00:52:08.790 --> 00:52:10.530
This place is huge!

1006
00:52:10.540 --> 00:52:13.030
Yeah, it looks so much smaller than I expected.

1007
00:52:13.790 --> 00:52:16.700
I can fly? I love that one!

1008
00:52:18.380 --> 00:52:20.450
Rainbow Unicorn! She's right there!

1009
00:52:23.390 --> 00:52:26.470
My friend says you're famous. She wants your autograph.

1010
00:52:26.470 --> 00:52:29.330
No, no, Sadness, don't bother Miss Unicorn, okay?

1011
00:52:29.350 --> 00:52:32.340
Sorry, she's from out of town. That was so embarrassing, right?

1012
00:52:33.560 --> 00:52:35.800
I loved you in Fairy Dream Adventure Part 7.

1013
00:52:35.820 --> 00:52:37.480
Okay, bye. I love you!

1014
00:52:38.740 --> 00:52:40.500
I wonder what that means.

1015
00:52:40.530 --> 00:52:41.750
Well, let's go in.

1016
00:52:43.950 --> 00:52:46.720
Set up the classroom set! Today's memories are in!

1017
00:52:46.740 --> 00:52:48.620
We've got a lot to work with here.

1018
00:52:48.660 --> 00:52:50.680
Riley dumped her best friend,

1019
00:52:50.680 --> 00:52:51.670
had a miserable day at school,

1020
00:52:51.710 --> 00:52:52.790
and quit hockey.

1021
00:52:52.790 --> 00:52:55.050
The writers have put together a killer script!

1022
00:52:55.090 --> 00:52:57.290
Just because Joy and Sadness are gone,

1023
00:52:57.300 --> 00:52:58.940
I have to do stupid dream duty.

1024
00:53:00.550 --> 00:53:02.690
Okay. How are we going to wake her up?

1025
00:53:02.720 --> 00:53:05.640
Well, she wakes up sometimes when she has a scary dream.

1026
00:53:05.640 --> 00:53:06.690
We could scare her.

1027
00:53:06.720 --> 00:53:09.020
Scare her? No, she's been through enough already.

1028
00:53:09.060 --> 00:53:10.140
- But, Joy...  - Sadness,

1029
00:53:10.140 --> 00:53:11.640
you may know your way around down here,

1030
00:53:11.640 --> 00:53:12.690
but I know Riley.

1031
00:53:12.730 --> 00:53:16.250
We're gonna make her so happy, she'll wake up with exhilaration.

1032
00:53:16.270 --> 00:53:17.610
We'll excite her awake!

1033
00:53:17.610 --> 00:53:19.750
That's never happened before.

1034
00:53:19.780 --> 00:53:21.420
Riley loves dogs. Put this on.

1035
00:53:21.440 --> 00:53:22.490
I don't think that'll work.

1036
00:53:22.490 --> 00:53:24.210
- Bing Bong?  - Yeah?

1037
00:53:24.240 --> 00:53:27.340
- Don't let anything happen to these.  - Got it.

1038
00:53:28.580 --> 00:53:30.800
Add the reality distortion filter.

1039
00:53:32.790 --> 00:53:35.710
Love it. Remember, play to the camera, everyone!

1040
00:53:35.750 --> 00:53:37.420
Riley is the camera!

